<mxfile host="app.diagrams.net"><diagram id="p_03_gate_tested_from_both_sides" name="03-gate-tested-from-both-sides"><mxGraphModel dx="800" dy="600" grid="0" gridSize="10" guides="1" tooltips="1" connect="1" arrows="1" fold="1" page="1" pageScale="1" pageWidth="1280" pageHeight="750" math="0" shadow="0"><root><mxCell id="0" /><mxCell id="1" parent="0" /><mxCell id="title" value="A gate is tested from both sides: the real baseline must PASS (the gate is not too tight) and every negative control must FAIL (the gate is not too loose)" style="text;html=0;whiteSpace=wrap;verticalAlign=middle;align=center;fontSize=17;fontStyle=1;fillColor=none;strokeColor=none;strokeWidth=1.5;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="20" y="12" width="1240" height="40" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="legit_h" value="MUST BE ACCEPTED" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;arcSize=16;verticalAlign=middle;align=center;fontSize=13;fontStyle=1;fillColor=#d5e8d4;strokeColor=#82b366;strokeWidth=1.5;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="30" y="70" width="330" height="34" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="bl" value="THE REAL BASELINE&#10;scheduling topic: accepted at binding 0.49 [I5] on the visible set, clearly below the cap 0.9 [I6]" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;arcSize=16;verticalAlign=middle;align=center;fontSize=11;fillColor=#d5e8d4;strokeColor=#82b366;strokeWidth=1.5;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="30" y="112" width="330" height="74" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="noise" value="LEGITIMATE-NOISE REFERENCES&#10;legitimate runs (e.g. reduced precision, another device) that set each limit, per input set (B1)" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;arcSize=16;verticalAlign=middle;align=center;fontSize=11;fillColor=#d5e8d4;strokeColor=#82b366;strokeWidth=1.5;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="30" y="196" width="330" height="74" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="tight" value="IF ONE IS REJECTED: the gate is too tight.&#10;In the first campaign the first gate rejected the real baseline; found the day the evaluator was built, because the baseline ran before any candidate." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;arcSize=16;verticalAlign=middle;align=left;fontSize=11;fillColor=#fff7f7;strokeColor=#b85450;strokeWidth=1.5;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="30" y="282" width="330" height="92" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="gate" value="THE FROZEN GATE (B2)&#10;is finished only when, on EVERY input set, held-out included:&#10;1. the baseline is ACCEPTED with margin clearly below 1&#10;2. every control is REJECTED&#10;&#10;re-run both on every evaluator version" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;arcSize=16;verticalAlign=middle;align=center;fontSize=12;fillColor=#ffe6cc;strokeColor=#d79b00;strokeWidth=1.5;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="450" y="150" width="380" height="150" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="ctrl_h" value="MUST BE REJECTED (negative controls)" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;arcSize=16;verticalAlign=middle;align=center;fontSize=13;fontStyle=1;fillColor=#f8cecc;strokeColor=#b85450;strokeWidth=1.5;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="920" y="70" width="330" height="34" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="c1" value="FIRST CAMPAIGN (diffusion-model policy)&#10;- fewer denoising steps -&gt; correctness gate vs reference&#10;- output scaled by 3 % [I1] -&gt; calibrated per-dimension limits&#10;- cached output -&gt; inputs change per call; 'model ran once'&#10;- perturbation on a second compute core -&gt; correctness gate" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;arcSize=16;verticalAlign=top;align=left;fontSize=11;fillColor=#fff7f7;strokeColor=#b85450;strokeWidth=1.5;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="920" y="112" width="330" height="128" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="c2" value="SCHEDULING TOPIC&#10;- starve_soft: never runs soft chains -&gt; completion check (logging, telemetry never finish)&#10;- not_ready: returns a job already started -&gt; integrity check&#10;- wallclock: unseeded random tie-break -&gt; order probe (REJECTED at 53.5 ms [I2])" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;arcSize=16;verticalAlign=top;align=left;fontSize=11;fillColor=#fff7f7;strokeColor=#b85450;strokeWidth=1.5;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="920" y="250" width="330" height="124" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="wrong" value="A CONTROL CAN BE WRONG TOO&#10;The wallclock control first salted its tie-break with the parity of a nanosecond clock. On the development machine that clock had microsecond resolution, so the parity was always even: the control was accidentally deterministic and the order probe could not see it. Fix: an unseeded random generator. Rule: run each control and confirm it fails for the reason it was built for." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;arcSize=16;verticalAlign=top;align=left;fontSize=11;fillColor=#f5f5f5;strokeColor=#999999;strokeWidth=1.5;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="30" y="400" width="600" height="92" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="hosts" value="DEVELOPMENT HOST vs EVALUATION HOST&#10;- development host: visible set only; its records are INVALID by design (scheduling topic quick mode: 4 seeds [I4]), so a development number is never taken for an official one&#10;- evaluation host: visible + held-out sets, official runs only&#10;- a device lock on each host keeps other work off the device during a timed run" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;arcSize=16;verticalAlign=top;align=left;fontSize=11;fillColor=#dae8fc;strokeColor=#6c8ebf;strokeWidth=1.5;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="650" y="400" width="600" height="92" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="popper" value="WHY: a claim is scientific only if some observation could refute it (Popper 1959 [P3]). A gate that has never rejected a plausible cheat makes no claim; the rejected controls are the observations that show it can refute. Most fake results are accidents (a bug that skips work looks like a cheat); controls catch both." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;arcSize=16;verticalAlign=middle;align=left;fontSize=11;fillColor=#e1d5e7;strokeColor=#9673a6;strokeWidth=1.5;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="30" y="504" width="1220" height="44" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="legend" value="Legend:  green = legitimate runs that must pass  |  red = controls that must fail, and the too-tight failure  |  amber = the frozen gate  |  blue = hosts  |  purple = the principle  |  arrow label = required verdict" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;arcSize=16;verticalAlign=middle;align=left;fontSize=11;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#999999;strokeWidth=1.5;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="30" y="560" width="1220" height="26" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="sources" value="Sources. Every number is loaded from ../constants.json by the key shown. [Pn] = public (cited paper, or my arithmetic on public mathematics); [In] = illustrative (a design parameter of the harness, a round value that keeps the shape of the first campaign, or output of the demonstration scheduling simulator; never a measurement of a real platform); [calc] = my arithmetic on tagged values.&#10;Mechanism: notes/B3-negative-controls.md (both control tables, 'a control can be wrong too', development vs evaluation host, device lock, Popper); notes/B2-the-frozen-evaluator.md; notes/B1-reference-and-baseline.md (legitimate-noise references); notes/C3-calibration.md (baseline binding, wallclock control rejected); notes/C4-lessons-about-the-method.md (gates fail both ways). The second-core perturbation's purpose is the notes' reading; the source names the control only.&#10;[I1] c1_control_scale_illustrative = 3 %. illustrative; keeps the shape of the first campaign (internal methodology notes, 2026), not its values&#10;[I2] sched_control_wallclock_ms = 53.5 ms. illustrative: demonstration run of the local scheduling simulator&#10;[P3] pub_popper_year = 1959 year. public: Popper, The Logic of Scientific Discovery, English edition, Hutchinson, 1959&#10;[I4] topic_quick_seeds = 4 seeds. illustrative: design parameter of the harness&#10;[I5] sched_baseline = {median 34.7, min 32.3, max 45.4, binding_visible 0.49, binding_a 0.34, binding_b 0.44} ms / binding. illustrative: demonstration run of the local scheduling simulator&#10;[I6] harness_margin_cap_scheduling = 0.9 binding ratio. illustrative: design parameter of the harness" style="text;html=0;whiteSpace=wrap;verticalAlign=top;align=left;fontSize=10;fillColor=#fff2cc;strokeColor=#d6b656;strokeWidth=1.5;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="30" y="598" width="1220" height="136" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="edge0" value="pass" style="endArrow=classic;html=0;fontSize=10;edgeStyle=none;fontStyle=1;strokeWidth=2;exitX=1;exitY=0.5;exitDx=0;exitDy=0;entryX=0;entryY=0.3;entryDx=0;entryDy=0;strokeColor=#82b366;fontColor=#82b366;" edge="1" parent="1" source="bl" target="gate"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"></mxGeometry></mxCell><mxCell id="edge1" value="pass" style="endArrow=classic;html=0;fontSize=10;edgeStyle=none;fontStyle=1;strokeWidth=2;exitX=1;exitY=0.5;exitDx=0;exitDy=0;entryX=0;entryY=0.6;entryDx=0;entryDy=0;strokeColor=#82b366;fontColor=#82b366;" edge="1" parent="1" source="noise" target="gate"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"></mxGeometry></mxCell><mxCell id="edge2" value="fail" style="endArrow=classic;html=0;fontSize=10;edgeStyle=none;fontStyle=1;strokeWidth=2;exitX=0;exitY=0.5;exitDx=0;exitDy=0;entryX=1;entryY=0.3;entryDx=0;entryDy=0;strokeColor=#b85450;fontColor=#b85450;" edge="1" parent="1" source="c1" target="gate"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"></mxGeometry></mxCell><mxCell id="edge3" value="fail" style="endArrow=classic;html=0;fontSize=10;edgeStyle=none;fontStyle=1;strokeWidth=2;exitX=0;exitY=0.5;exitDx=0;exitDy=0;entryX=1;entryY=0.7;entryDx=0;entryDy=0;strokeColor=#b85450;fontColor=#b85450;" edge="1" parent="1" source="c2" target="gate"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"></mxGeometry></mxCell></root></mxGraphModel></diagram></mxfile>